1
00:00:33,241 --> 00:00:37,954
‪AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

2
00:00:50,675 --> 00:00:52,844
‪You took a hit,
‪so it's only right you return the favor.

3
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:58,183
‪Thank you for giving me a chance
‪to redeem myself.

4
00:01:03,813 --> 00:01:05,899
‪PERSONAL RECORD
‪NAME: PARK JIN-CHEOL

5
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:07,734
‪PERSONAL RECORD
‪NAME: SUNG HAN-SOO

6
00:01:11,654 --> 00:01:12,489
‪I'm listening.

7
00:01:12,572 --> 00:01:13,406
‪A FEW HOURS AGO

8
00:01:16,034 --> 00:01:18,536
‪Why don't we stir things up even more?

9
00:01:21,498 --> 00:01:25,335
‪INTER-KOREAN GOVERNMENT TALKS

10
00:01:26,377 --> 00:01:28,713
‪This is just ridiculous.

11
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:33,092
‪ASSEMBLYMAN SIM JONG-SEON, PRIME MINISTER

12
00:01:35,678 --> 00:01:36,513
‪What?

13
00:01:38,473 --> 00:01:39,682
<i>‪Please explain.</i>

14
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:42,644
‪Why do you
‪suddenly want to cancel the talks?

15
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:48,650
‪It's entirely because the South
‪isn't prepared to engage in the talks.

16
00:01:48,733 --> 00:01:50,568
‪What do you mean?

17
00:01:50,652 --> 00:01:54,781
‪You run your mouth
‪about peaceful talks and cooperation,

18
00:01:54,864 --> 00:01:58,243
‪but you're stabbing our regime
‪in the back.

19
00:01:58,326 --> 00:01:59,160
‪What did you say?

20
00:01:59,744 --> 00:02:01,579
‪You think we don't know?

21
00:02:03,331 --> 00:02:06,084
‪I'm talking about
‪Director General Ri Eung Ryeong.

22
00:02:06,751 --> 00:02:09,879
‪As if it wasn't bad enough
‪that the South intercepted him,

23
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:12,882
‪the Republic's most wanted fugitive
‪has been assigned to protect him.

24
00:02:18,638 --> 00:02:19,848
‪I'll cut to the chase.

25
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:23,977
‪If you don't hand over
‪those two traitors immediately,

26
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:26,104
‪not only will we cancel the talks,

27
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:31,401
‪but the relationship between our countries
‪will change drastically.

28
00:02:39,617 --> 00:02:41,369
‪Contact General Jang right now.

29
00:02:41,452 --> 00:02:42,370
‪Yes, sir.

30
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:44,831
‪EPISODE 9

31
00:02:44,914 --> 00:02:47,375
‪ONCE A MARINE, ALWAYS A MARINE
‪KOREAN MARINE VETERANS FEDERATION

32
00:03:02,015 --> 00:03:03,016
‪You failed…

33
00:03:04,517 --> 00:03:05,393
‪your mission.

34
00:03:21,326 --> 00:03:25,830
‪It was so satisfying to see
‪the prime minister of South Korea

35
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:28,166
‪tuck his tail between his legs.

36
00:03:29,167 --> 00:03:31,794
‪Things worked out easily, thanks to you.

37
00:03:34,213 --> 00:03:36,466
‪Now it's your turn to do me a favor.

38
00:03:36,549 --> 00:03:38,551
‪I always keep my promises.

39
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,054
‪But there's a catch.

40
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:46,476
‪You must be alone, Comrade Ju.

41
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:49,979
‪Given that the matter
‪has been officially settled,

42
00:03:50,605 --> 00:03:53,691
‪killing 66 on South Korean soil

43
00:03:54,317 --> 00:03:55,610
‪will put us in an uncomfortable position.

44
00:03:57,737 --> 00:03:59,072
‪There's no need to worry about that.

45
00:04:55,461 --> 00:04:57,213
<i>‪What do you mean, sir?</i>

46
00:04:57,297 --> 00:05:00,049
‪Until we secure
‪the ballistic missile information,

47
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:01,968
‪Ri Eung Ryeong must not be eliminated.

48
00:05:02,051 --> 00:05:03,970
‪The mission has already failed.

49
00:05:04,804 --> 00:05:06,347
‪Are you disobeying

50
00:05:07,598 --> 00:05:08,558
‪the prime minister's orders?

51
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:12,186
‪We're turning 66 and Ri Eung Ryeong

52
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:13,771
‪over to the North.

53
00:05:15,565 --> 00:05:19,694
<i>‪But if 66 continues to act on his own,</i>

54
00:05:20,695 --> 00:05:22,530
<i>‪it has nothing to do with us, does it?</i>

55
00:05:23,489 --> 00:05:26,701
<i>‪All we have to do is sit back and watch.</i>

56
00:05:34,083 --> 00:05:37,628
<i>‪He'll do anything</i>

57
00:05:37,712 --> 00:05:39,589
<i>‪to see his daughter again.</i>

58
00:05:46,679 --> 00:05:48,556
‪AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

59
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:51,309
‪Hey, about that Ass Cricket.

60
00:05:52,226 --> 00:05:53,603
‪He handcuffed Kim, right?

61
00:05:54,479 --> 00:05:55,354
‪Yeah.

62
00:05:56,022 --> 00:05:58,274
‪Knowing full well that won't stop him?

63
00:05:59,692 --> 00:06:00,526
‪Yeah.

64
00:06:02,945 --> 00:06:04,906
‪I guess we don't have to help him, then.

65
00:06:10,244 --> 00:06:12,246
‪But wouldn't it be hard for him to return?

66
00:06:12,872 --> 00:06:15,500
‪He's dealing with serious people,
‪not local thugs.

67
00:06:23,007 --> 00:06:23,841
‪Are you going?

68
00:06:24,467 --> 00:06:25,301
‪What about you?

69
00:06:32,975 --> 00:06:34,644
‪The punk left his phone behind.

70
00:06:35,645 --> 00:06:37,396
‪And he took mine instead.

71
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,731
‪What? He took yours?

72
00:06:38,815 --> 00:06:40,233
‪Yeah, he took mine.

73
00:06:40,316 --> 00:06:42,110
‪What was he thinking?

74
00:06:42,193 --> 00:06:43,903
‪I should go and get mine back.

75
00:06:44,487 --> 00:06:46,656
‪Of course, you should.
‪Your phone is more expensive.

76
00:06:47,573 --> 00:06:49,117
‪I'm not done paying it off either.

77
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,077
‪Then what are you waiting for?

78
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:53,121
‪Why, that jerk…

79
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:54,038
‪Hold on!

80
00:06:54,747 --> 00:06:55,957
‪Before we go,

81
00:06:57,708 --> 00:06:59,168
‪let's have one of these.

82
00:06:59,252 --> 00:07:00,128
‪What's this?

83
00:07:00,211 --> 00:07:01,379
‪It's good for your joints.

84
00:07:01,462 --> 00:07:03,506
‪And you didn't think
‪to share this with me before?

85
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:04,841
‪Why would I?

86
00:07:10,763 --> 00:07:11,639
‪Let's go.

87
00:07:13,224 --> 00:07:14,142
‪Where's the car?

88
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:16,811
‪Hey, what's this car?

89
00:07:16,894 --> 00:07:17,895
‪This?

90
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:19,355
‪A next-generation car.

91
00:07:19,439 --> 00:07:21,691
‪A next-generation car, huh?

92
00:07:21,774 --> 00:07:22,984
‪Let's see how it drives.

93
00:07:27,363 --> 00:07:29,740
‪Damn it, it's the hero
‪who should be driving!

94
00:08:01,856 --> 00:08:03,608
‪We sent 66 ahead to be taken care of.

95
00:08:05,693 --> 00:08:07,778
‪It's nice to handle this
‪without getting our hands dirty.

96
00:08:07,862 --> 00:08:10,156
<i>‪Report to the South and the Party</i>

97
00:08:10,239 --> 00:08:14,410
<i>‪that both Ri Eung Ryeong and 66</i>
<i>‪were subjected to summary execution.</i>

98
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:15,453
‪Yes, sir.

99
00:08:39,977 --> 00:08:41,896
‪Goodbye, you traitorous bastard.

100
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:43,564
<i>‪Son of a bitch.</i>

101
00:09:17,557 --> 00:09:19,392
‪I had no idea you were such a big deal.

102
00:09:20,351 --> 00:09:23,813
‪I'm sorry
‪I didn't treat you better last time.

103
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:26,566
‪You promised to turn yourself in.

104
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:30,570
‪Our parent meeting isn't over yet.

105
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:37,785
‪So you're the rat bastard
‪who teamed up with the North.

106
00:09:37,868 --> 00:09:39,370
‪You're the rat bastard.

107
00:09:40,746 --> 00:09:43,249
‪The rat bastard who betrayed his country.

108
00:09:47,878 --> 00:09:49,380
‪We have a lot in common.

109
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:54,135
‪We're both good dads who would do anything

110
00:09:55,219 --> 00:09:56,178
‪for our children.

111
00:09:57,513 --> 00:09:58,598
‪Don't you agree?

112
00:09:59,473 --> 00:10:02,059
‪You said you'd end me
‪for the sake of your daughter.

113
00:10:04,645 --> 00:10:06,981
‪I'll do the same for my daughter
‪and end you.

114
00:10:24,332 --> 00:10:25,541
‪But not here.

115
00:10:29,086 --> 00:10:30,046
‪Put him in the trunk.

116
00:10:53,194 --> 00:10:54,028
‪Comrade.

117
00:10:59,116 --> 00:11:00,534
‪You have a really nice car.

118
00:11:09,251 --> 00:11:10,252
‪Go to sleep.

119
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:13,255
‪I didn't really come here to help you.

120
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:14,840
‪Jeez.

121
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:16,967
‪I came to bring you your phone,

122
00:11:17,051 --> 00:11:19,220
‪but the gunshots were so loud,

123
00:11:19,303 --> 00:11:20,596
‪so I ended up stepping in.

124
00:11:21,722 --> 00:11:22,556
‪Thanks.

125
00:11:24,016 --> 00:11:26,727
‪So now what?
‪Ri Eung Ryeong is probably dead by now.

126
00:11:26,811 --> 00:11:28,020
‪I don't think so.

127
00:11:28,104 --> 00:11:29,563
‪They tried to take him alive.

128
00:11:29,647 --> 00:11:30,648
‪Really?

129
00:11:30,731 --> 00:11:32,608
‪This guy is really something else,

130
00:11:32,691 --> 00:11:34,485
‪teaming up with the North.

131
00:11:34,568 --> 00:11:36,987
‪I thought he was just an asshole,

132
00:11:37,071 --> 00:11:38,906
‪but he's a snake too.

133
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:42,451
‪Where did they take Ri Eung Ryeong?

134
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:49,166
‪Go ahead and shoot me

135
00:11:49,917 --> 00:11:52,128
‪if you want to leave our kids fatherless.

136
00:11:52,211 --> 00:11:53,045
‪Shoot him.

137
00:11:53,921 --> 00:11:55,005
‪You actually fired.

138
00:12:00,428 --> 00:12:01,262
‪Let's make a deal.

139
00:12:02,930 --> 00:12:05,182
‪I know why
‪you're looking for Ri Eung Ryeong.

140
00:12:06,392 --> 00:12:07,476
‪If you let me live,

141
00:12:08,811 --> 00:12:10,020
‪I'll help you find him.

142
00:12:19,822 --> 00:12:20,948
‪Let's go.

143
00:12:22,366 --> 00:12:23,701
‪You'd better not be lying.

144
00:12:26,745 --> 00:12:28,789
‪Sleep well and sweet dreams.

145
00:12:32,543 --> 00:12:33,377
‪Han-soo.

146
00:12:34,295 --> 00:12:35,129
‪Thanks.

147
00:12:38,048 --> 00:12:41,218
‪We want to see Min-ji walk down the aisle.

148
00:12:46,432 --> 00:12:47,266
‪Let's go.

149
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:38,359
‪HOTEL

150
00:13:40,402 --> 00:13:41,445
‪It's the North Koreans' car!

151
00:13:41,529 --> 00:13:43,531
‪SECURITY CHECK

152
00:13:54,792 --> 00:13:56,168
‪Let them in!

153
00:13:56,752 --> 00:13:57,962
‪Maintain tight security.

154
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:08,889
‪You've got to be kidding me.

155
00:14:08,973 --> 00:14:10,432
‪We're not their damn subordinates.

156
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:11,475
‪Just let it go.

157
00:14:12,059 --> 00:14:14,728
‪I think our government is indulging them.

158
00:14:14,812 --> 00:14:16,689
‪It makes no sense
‪to ban us from the inside

159
00:14:16,772 --> 00:14:19,775
‪and only use us for perimeter security.

160
00:14:19,858 --> 00:14:20,693
‪Did you forget

161
00:14:20,776 --> 00:14:23,696
‪they're the most closed-off country
‪in the world?

162
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:24,655
‪That place right there

163
00:14:25,281 --> 00:14:26,156
‪is basically North Korea.

164
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:41,422
‪DIPLOMATIC POUCH
‪DPRK, MINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS

165
00:14:41,505 --> 00:14:42,882
‪WE WELCOME THE NORTH KOREAN DELEGATION
‪TO JUHAK HERITAGE RESORT

166
00:14:44,717 --> 00:14:47,303
‪Jongilbong 25 has arrived
‪at the reception hall.

167
00:14:53,225 --> 00:14:55,561
<i>‪Jongilbong 25 is on Elevator 3.</i>

168
00:14:59,815 --> 00:15:01,942
‪Jongilbong 25 has arrived
‪on the 5th floor.

169
00:15:07,072 --> 00:15:09,658
<i>‪Jongilbong 25</i>
<i>‪is approaching the VIP suite.</i>

170
00:15:11,410 --> 00:15:14,288
<i>‪Jongilbong 25</i>
<i>‪has arrived at the VIP suite.</i>

171
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:16,916
‪Status report, sir.

172
00:15:16,999 --> 00:15:19,460
‪No, I'll report directly.

173
00:15:57,289 --> 00:16:00,209
‪Goodness, Comrade Director General.

174
00:16:00,292 --> 00:16:02,252
‪You look terrible.

175
00:16:02,962 --> 00:16:05,172
‪Things must've been tough away from home.

176
00:16:07,675 --> 00:16:11,261
‪Cut to the chase and get it over with.

177
00:16:11,345 --> 00:16:13,263
‪What's the rush?

178
00:16:13,347 --> 00:16:14,765
‪We still have plenty of time.

179
00:16:20,145 --> 00:16:25,859
‪The first thing you should do is tell me
‪how much information about the missiles

180
00:16:25,943 --> 00:16:28,237
‪you've spilled
‪to the South Korean puppet regime.

181
00:16:29,989 --> 00:16:31,365
‪Fill the bathtub.

182
00:16:44,795 --> 00:16:45,879
‪What happened?

183
00:16:45,963 --> 00:16:48,465
‪A North Korean vehicle
‪arrived at the resort just now,

184
00:16:49,049 --> 00:16:52,052
‪and we spotted them
‪moving a large bag inside.

185
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:10,738
<i>‪It's Ri Eung Ryeong.</i>

186
00:17:11,405 --> 00:17:12,740
<i>‪Military police secure the perimeter,</i>

187
00:17:12,823 --> 00:17:15,325
<i>‪while NIS agents</i>
<i>‪stand guard on the inside.</i>

188
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:17,619
<i>‪The NIS agents have access to areas</i>
<i>‪where domestic staff work,</i>

189
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:19,830
<i>‪like the kitchen or laundry room.</i>

190
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:23,459
<i>‪But they're under constant surveillance</i>
<i>‪by North Korean agents.</i>

191
00:17:24,501 --> 00:17:25,836
‪This won't be easy.

192
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:27,463
‪-Hey, mister.
‪-Want to see?

193
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:29,506
‪Which floors is the North staying on?

194
00:17:30,090 --> 00:17:31,133
‪The fourth and fifth floors.

195
00:17:31,759 --> 00:17:34,178
‪So the North Korean delegation head
‪is on the fifth floor,

196
00:17:34,261 --> 00:17:36,472
‪and they probably set up
‪a surveillance room on the fourth.

197
00:17:37,306 --> 00:17:38,766
‪That's how they do things.

198
00:17:39,725 --> 00:17:41,018
‪How are we going to get in?

199
00:17:50,861 --> 00:17:51,695
‪Hey.

200
00:17:52,321 --> 00:17:54,531
‪Is there an easy way to get in?

201
00:17:54,615 --> 00:17:56,450
‪Come on, you really think he'll talk?

202
00:17:57,034 --> 00:17:58,494
‪The condition is very simple.

203
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:00,621
‪If we extract Ri Eung Ryeong,

204
00:18:01,455 --> 00:18:02,289
‪you live.

205
00:18:03,123 --> 00:18:04,458
‪If we fail, you die.

206
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:12,382
‪There's a passage that goes straight
‪to the chairman's office.

207
00:18:13,383 --> 00:18:15,511
‪It was built for emergencies,
‪so there's no CCTV either.

208
00:18:15,594 --> 00:18:16,845
‪Really?

209
00:18:16,929 --> 00:18:19,181
‪Hold on, it can't be that easy.

210
00:18:19,264 --> 00:18:20,808
‪Let me take a look at you.

211
00:18:20,891 --> 00:18:21,975
‪How do we get through the barricades?

212
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:25,896
‪I have clearance…

213
00:18:25,979 --> 00:18:27,606
‪CARD ID: JU GANG-CHAN

214
00:18:27,689 --> 00:18:28,774
‪…since I'm in charge of protocol.

215
00:18:30,317 --> 00:18:31,401
‪Easier than I expected.

216
00:18:34,238 --> 00:18:37,282
‪We'll locate Ri Eung Ryeong
‪through the CCTVs

217
00:18:37,366 --> 00:18:38,784
‪once we get to the chairman's room.

218
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:41,161
‪There's a problem though.

219
00:18:41,662 --> 00:18:43,664
<i>‪They've disabled all the existing CCTVs</i>

220
00:18:43,747 --> 00:18:47,417
<i>‪and are running their own</i>
<i>‪from the surveillance room.</i>

221
00:18:47,501 --> 00:18:50,921
‪We basically need to secure
‪the surveillance room.

222
00:18:51,004 --> 00:18:53,465
‪Once we seize the surveillance room
‪and locate Ri Eung Ryeong,

223
00:18:53,549 --> 00:18:56,051
‪I'll go in and secure him.

224
00:18:56,135 --> 00:18:57,970
‪Then while you escape,

225
00:18:58,554 --> 00:18:59,888
‪we'll keep them distracted.

226
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:02,307
‪-Me too.
‪-Hold on.

227
00:19:03,058 --> 00:19:04,268
‪Getting that man

228
00:19:04,852 --> 00:19:06,770
‪and leaving through the front entrance

229
00:19:06,854 --> 00:19:08,313
‪won't be easy.

230
00:19:09,189 --> 00:19:11,650
‪We'll smuggle him in a laundry truck

231
00:19:11,733 --> 00:19:13,318
‪through the first-floor loading dock.

232
00:19:13,402 --> 00:19:14,903
‪A laundry truck?

233
00:19:14,987 --> 00:19:17,197
‪Laundry is my specialty,
‪so I'll handle that.

234
00:19:17,865 --> 00:19:20,534
<i>‪The laundry truck arrives at 7:20 p.m.</i>

235
00:19:20,617 --> 00:19:23,912
‪It leaves at 7:30 p.m. after pickup.

236
00:19:23,996 --> 00:19:26,165
‪You'll only have ten minutes.
‪It won't be easy.

237
00:19:26,248 --> 00:19:27,082
‪We have ten minutes

238
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:31,378
‪to locate, secure,
‪and get him to the loading dock.

239
00:19:31,461 --> 00:19:33,797
‪That's easier said than done.

240
00:19:34,381 --> 00:19:36,049
‪They check in every three minutes.

241
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:37,676
‪This won't be easy.

242
00:19:37,759 --> 00:19:39,219
‪We already know it won't be easy.

243
00:19:39,303 --> 00:19:40,888
‪Stop saying that.

244
00:19:40,971 --> 00:19:42,931
‪Why are you so negative? You scared?

245
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:44,766
‪Look, you've only been on
‪the Taekwondo demo team,

246
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:46,602
‪-so you probably don't know much.
‪-Stop bringing that up.

247
00:19:46,685 --> 00:19:47,895
‪-It's not that easy--
‪-Anyway.

248
00:19:47,978 --> 00:19:49,855
‪We'll be ready, just in case.

249
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:54,443
‪We'll leave the same way we came in.

250
00:19:57,237 --> 00:19:59,031
‪We need to get through
‪the barricades first.

251
00:20:00,073 --> 00:20:02,367
‪Let's get geared up.

252
00:20:27,517 --> 00:20:29,228
‪You need to conceal your wounds.

253
00:20:33,649 --> 00:20:34,775
‪We're missing something.

254
00:20:36,193 --> 00:20:37,027
‪A tranquilizer gun.

255
00:20:37,110 --> 00:20:38,654
‪Just use them all up!

256
00:20:38,737 --> 00:20:39,821
‪Enough…

257
00:20:40,781 --> 00:20:42,115
‪Sorry about that.

258
00:20:45,202 --> 00:20:46,203
‪Peace.

259
00:20:46,745 --> 00:20:49,122
‪I'll keep you posted
‪on the situation outside.

260
00:20:49,206 --> 00:20:51,208
‪Be careful, everyone.

261
00:20:51,291 --> 00:20:53,001
‪You shot me four times.

262
00:21:00,926 --> 00:21:02,344
‪You can manage, right?

263
00:21:03,136 --> 00:21:04,930
‪I told you I didn't want to play
‪rock-paper-scissors.

264
00:21:06,515 --> 00:21:07,474
‪You did.

265
00:21:09,476 --> 00:21:10,435
‪You guys planned this!

266
00:21:10,519 --> 00:21:12,145
‪-How fun.
‪-You planned this!

267
00:21:13,313 --> 00:21:14,856
‪You both played scissors at the same time!

268
00:21:29,871 --> 00:21:30,706
‪AUTHORIZED VEHICLE
‪JU GANG-CHAN

269
00:21:30,789 --> 00:21:32,708
‪Ju Gang-chan.
‪He's the chairman of this resort.

270
00:21:46,471 --> 00:21:47,973
‪What's the purpose of your visit?

271
00:21:51,893 --> 00:21:53,520
‪He's here for protocol arrangements.

272
00:21:55,439 --> 00:21:56,356
‪Have you heard about this?

273
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:57,774
‪No, sir.

274
00:22:02,988 --> 00:22:04,448
‪Please lower the rear window.

275
00:22:13,707 --> 00:22:16,043
‪I'm here on the orders
‪of the vice minister of National Security.

276
00:22:16,126 --> 00:22:17,461
‪You can check.

277
00:22:17,544 --> 00:22:18,754
‪Just a moment, please.

278
00:22:22,507 --> 00:22:25,135
‪Chairman Ju says he's here
‪for protocol arrangements.

279
00:22:25,218 --> 00:22:27,012
‪Please verify this with the vice minister.

280
00:22:33,685 --> 00:22:34,936
‪Okay, thank you.

281
00:22:37,272 --> 00:22:38,106
‪Here you go, sir.

282
00:22:39,066 --> 00:22:39,941
‪Let them in.

283
00:22:40,817 --> 00:22:41,777
‪Move the barricades.

284
00:23:09,262 --> 00:23:11,056
‪Oh gosh, my knees.

285
00:23:15,435 --> 00:23:16,353
‪Man, my knees.

286
00:24:01,314 --> 00:24:02,149
‪Hey.

287
00:24:03,024 --> 00:24:06,528
‪Are you trying to let people know
‪that we came through here?

288
00:24:08,071 --> 00:24:09,531
‪RESTRICTED AREA
‪NO ENTRY

289
00:24:23,712 --> 00:24:25,547
‪ACCESS RESTRICTED

290
00:24:25,630 --> 00:24:26,464
‪GRANTED

291
00:24:31,386 --> 00:24:34,556
‪JUHAK HERITAGE RESORT

292
00:24:55,911 --> 00:24:57,370
‪ACCESS RESTRICTED

293
00:24:57,454 --> 00:24:58,330
‪GRANTED

294
00:25:01,208 --> 00:25:03,460
‪Wow, fingerprint recognition, huh?

295
00:25:04,336 --> 00:25:06,296
‪Did you install this just for yourself?

296
00:25:06,379 --> 00:25:08,840
‪-Why?
‪-Why do you think?

297
00:25:08,924 --> 00:25:13,386
‪People with dirty secrets always make sure
‪they have an escape route.

298
00:25:14,221 --> 00:25:15,430
‪-Typical.
‪-Typical.

299
00:25:15,513 --> 00:25:16,723
‪-Jeez.
‪-Jeez.

300
00:25:16,806 --> 00:25:17,766
‪Jeez.

301
00:25:22,604 --> 00:25:23,438
‪Go.

302
00:25:29,110 --> 00:25:32,447
‪Man, this door is straight out of a drama.

303
00:25:32,530 --> 00:25:34,115
‪Why would he make this?

304
00:25:34,199 --> 00:25:36,243
‪Because he has dirty secrets.

305
00:25:36,326 --> 00:25:37,535
‪Man, look at this place.

306
00:25:37,619 --> 00:25:39,371
‪It's nice.

307
00:25:39,454 --> 00:25:41,164
‪You want to switch offices with me?

308
00:25:43,250 --> 00:25:44,251
‪Get the resort blueprints.

309
00:25:48,004 --> 00:25:49,506
‪Three minutes
‪to secure the surveillance room.

310
00:25:49,589 --> 00:25:51,091
‪No, two minutes.

311
00:25:51,174 --> 00:25:53,718
‪This is where I can infiltrate.

312
00:25:53,802 --> 00:25:54,886
‪How long?

313
00:25:55,637 --> 00:25:57,597
‪I think two minutes is enough

314
00:25:58,181 --> 00:25:59,474
‪to get to the loading dock.

315
00:26:00,100 --> 00:26:01,434
‪Will you be all right, Sang-a?

316
00:26:01,518 --> 00:26:02,644
‪I'll figure it out.

317
00:26:03,645 --> 00:26:05,272
‪We'll distract them
‪from the opposite side.

318
00:26:06,481 --> 00:26:08,650
‪If all this goes as planned,

319
00:26:08,733 --> 00:26:12,362
‪we'll meet back here
‪in the chairman's office.

320
00:26:13,488 --> 00:26:14,823
‪How about you put the gun away?

321
00:26:15,991 --> 00:26:17,742
‪You shouldn't treat a civilian like this.

322
00:26:20,245 --> 00:26:23,415
‪Besides, no one will hear me,
‪no matter how loud I yell.

323
00:26:23,498 --> 00:26:24,332
‪Oh, yeah?

324
00:26:29,379 --> 00:26:31,339
‪-Let's get started, Jin-cheol.
‪-You're no fun.

325
00:26:36,636 --> 00:26:37,470
‪Testing.

326
00:26:38,346 --> 00:26:39,389
‪All right.

327
00:26:40,181 --> 00:26:41,266
‪It's me.

328
00:26:42,058 --> 00:26:43,226
‪I want to order room service.

329
00:26:44,269 --> 00:26:45,395
<i>‪Ready, sir.</i>

330
00:26:45,478 --> 00:26:46,604
‪What can you prepare right now?

331
00:26:52,986 --> 00:26:53,820
‪Yes?

332
00:26:55,822 --> 00:26:56,656
‪Come in.

333
00:27:18,053 --> 00:27:19,637
‪What size do you wear?

334
00:27:20,221 --> 00:27:21,806
‪I wear a 3XL.

335
00:27:22,432 --> 00:27:23,350
‪That's a bit small.

336
00:27:29,397 --> 00:27:31,441
‪I feel awkward in this chef's jacket.

337
00:27:32,275 --> 00:27:34,778
‪I'll move the second you locate
‪Ri Eung Ryeong.

338
00:27:35,362 --> 00:27:36,780
‪Watch your back.

339
00:27:36,863 --> 00:27:37,947
‪-You too.
‪-How do I look?

340
00:27:38,031 --> 00:27:38,990
‪You managed to squeeze into it.

341
00:27:39,074 --> 00:27:40,658
‪That's right. Now it's your turn.

342
00:27:41,451 --> 00:27:44,371
‪-Come on, I'm not a contortionist.
‪-We don't have time.

343
00:27:44,454 --> 00:27:46,331
‪Why do I always have to
‪squeeze into things?

344
00:27:46,414 --> 00:27:50,085
‪-Mr. Park Jin-cheol won't fit in there.
‪-What am I, origami paper?

345
00:27:50,168 --> 00:27:52,629
‪I keep getting folded up and shoved in.

346
00:27:53,463 --> 00:27:55,840
‪-I'll join the circus at this rate.
‪-Let's go.

347
00:27:55,924 --> 00:27:56,758
‪Be quiet.

348
00:28:29,416 --> 00:28:31,668
‪I didn't know South Korean comrades
‪were so pretty.

349
00:28:31,751 --> 00:28:33,211
‪My, she's beautiful.

350
00:28:41,511 --> 00:28:42,929
‪Hello there.

351
00:28:43,513 --> 00:28:44,806
‪I'm here to pick up the laundry.

352
00:28:44,889 --> 00:28:45,724
‪INTER-KOREAN TALKS
‪AUTHORIZED VEHICLE

353
00:28:45,807 --> 00:28:47,809
‪CARD ID: JEONG JAE-WOOK

354
00:28:50,979 --> 00:28:51,813
‪Have a good one.

355
00:28:52,439 --> 00:28:53,440
‪Let him in!

356
00:28:53,523 --> 00:28:54,691
‪Thank you.

357
00:28:56,985 --> 00:28:58,695
‪LAUNDRY HUB

358
00:29:09,914 --> 00:29:10,999
‪Who is it?

359
00:29:11,082 --> 00:29:12,542
‪Room service, sir.

360
00:29:14,377 --> 00:29:15,795
‪Is it already time to eat?

361
00:29:16,546 --> 00:29:17,881
‪They're a little early.

362
00:29:17,964 --> 00:29:19,924
‪I'm hungry. Let's just eat.

363
00:29:34,397 --> 00:29:35,440
‪I think we work well together.

364
00:29:35,523 --> 00:29:37,025
‪My knees aren't working well though.

365
00:29:37,692 --> 00:29:38,902
‪Surveillance room secured.

366
00:29:51,664 --> 00:29:53,666
‪Oh, hello!

367
00:29:55,210 --> 00:29:57,378
‪No, let's look at the file
‪before that one.

368
00:29:57,462 --> 00:29:58,546
‪It's not here, see?

369
00:29:58,630 --> 00:30:00,924
‪-Why won't you listen to me?
‪-Be quiet, will you?

370
00:30:01,007 --> 00:30:02,592
‪You're making it hard to find anything.

371
00:30:02,675 --> 00:30:04,010
‪This is so frustrating.

372
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:06,930
‪Let's take a look at this one.

373
00:30:08,306 --> 00:30:09,766
‪Right there!

374
00:30:11,810 --> 00:30:13,394
‪I think this is the bag.

375
00:30:13,478 --> 00:30:15,063
‪-What is it?
‪-Let's follow it.

376
00:30:21,402 --> 00:30:22,403
‪Where is it?

377
00:30:22,487 --> 00:30:24,239
‪-Where is this place?
‪-The fifth-floor suite.

378
00:30:56,855 --> 00:30:58,022
‪Stop.

379
00:31:04,612 --> 00:31:05,572
‪I told you

380
00:31:06,322 --> 00:31:10,076
‪that I didn't reveal any information.

381
00:31:10,952 --> 00:31:14,747
‪I haven't even met
‪with the South Korean authorities!

382
00:31:16,165 --> 00:31:20,628
‪So you don't count 66
‪as a South Korean official?

383
00:31:21,921 --> 00:31:22,964
‪Continue.

384
00:31:26,134 --> 00:31:27,093
‪Comrade, sir!

385
00:31:33,349 --> 00:31:34,392
‪What is it?

386
00:31:34,475 --> 00:31:36,728
‪The agents sent to eliminate 66
‪have gone missing.

387
00:31:37,312 --> 00:31:39,689
‪What? 66…

388
00:31:40,273 --> 00:31:41,357
‪I'm sure he'll come here.

389
00:31:41,441 --> 00:31:43,902
‪Those South Korean bastards are outside,

390
00:31:43,985 --> 00:31:46,237
‪-so no shooting unless necessary.
‪-Yes, sir.

391
00:31:46,321 --> 00:31:47,697
‪-Follow me.
‪-Yes, sir.

392
00:31:53,870 --> 00:31:55,246
‪Should we continue, sir?

393
00:31:56,497 --> 00:31:57,582
‪Bring him out.

394
00:32:03,796 --> 00:32:04,631
<i>‪Hey, Kim.</i>

395
00:32:05,298 --> 00:32:06,382
<i>‪How much longer?</i>

396
00:32:06,466 --> 00:32:08,843
‪You think he's in a position
‪to talk right now?

397
00:32:08,927 --> 00:32:11,471
‪Maybe this hero
‪should've led the infiltration instead.

398
00:32:12,347 --> 00:32:13,723
‪We're running out of time.

399
00:32:14,599 --> 00:32:15,433
‪Sit down.

400
00:32:15,516 --> 00:32:17,894
‪Damn it, these guys will catch on soon.

401
00:32:20,104 --> 00:32:21,773
‪Comrades, leave the room.

402
00:32:21,856 --> 00:32:22,982
‪Sir?

403
00:32:23,066 --> 00:32:24,692
‪I said leave the room.

404
00:32:26,319 --> 00:32:27,195
‪Yes, sir.

405
00:32:39,582 --> 00:32:42,001
‪The two agents who just left
‪are standing by the door.

406
00:32:42,085 --> 00:32:42,919
‪Got it.

407
00:32:43,586 --> 00:32:45,296
‪What do you want from me?

408
00:32:56,391 --> 00:32:58,518
‪I believe you, Comrade Ri Eung Ryeong.

409
00:32:58,601 --> 00:33:02,772
‪To be honest, I don't care what happens
‪to the missile information.

410
00:33:03,439 --> 00:33:07,735
‪I'm going to give you a chance to live.

411
00:33:17,829 --> 00:33:22,083
‪About the funds you funneled to Macau
‪for operations against the South.

412
00:33:23,418 --> 00:33:25,336
‪You converted
‪eight million dollars into chips

413
00:33:25,420 --> 00:33:28,506
‪and stored them in a private safe
‪at the Fanta Casino.

414
00:33:29,507 --> 00:33:31,551
‪Just hand over the safe's access card.

415
00:33:31,634 --> 00:33:33,302
‪Then I'll arrange for you

416
00:33:33,386 --> 00:33:35,471
‪to be smuggled into a third country.

417
00:33:46,899 --> 00:33:48,860
‪Just as I expected.

418
00:33:49,694 --> 00:33:55,074
‪This is why you kept me alive.

419
00:33:57,035 --> 00:33:59,954
‪Where's the access card?

420
00:34:00,038 --> 00:34:02,290
‪If I hand that over right now,

421
00:34:02,373 --> 00:34:05,251
‪then how can I make a deal with you?

422
00:34:06,169 --> 00:34:09,338
‪I knew something like this might happen,

423
00:34:09,422 --> 00:34:11,507
‪so I hid it in China

424
00:34:12,425 --> 00:34:13,926
‪before coming to the South.

425
00:34:14,635 --> 00:34:16,012
‪Don't bullshit me.

426
00:34:16,721 --> 00:34:18,389
‪This isn't a deal.

427
00:34:18,890 --> 00:34:21,768
‪I have the authority
‪to execute you on the spot.

428
00:34:23,394 --> 00:34:24,687
‪This is your last chance.

429
00:34:24,771 --> 00:34:26,147
‪Tell me.

430
00:34:26,230 --> 00:34:27,732
‪Where's the access card?

431
00:34:37,075 --> 00:34:38,868
‪I knew it.

432
00:34:38,951 --> 00:34:40,745
‪I'd expect no less from you, 66.

433
00:34:41,913 --> 00:34:46,209
‪You're truly the regime's finest warrior.

434
00:34:46,834 --> 00:34:48,377
‪-No, you're--
‪-Be quiet

435
00:34:49,003 --> 00:34:50,171
‪if you want to live.

436
00:34:54,675 --> 00:34:55,676
‪Ri Eung Ryeong secured.

437
00:34:59,597 --> 00:35:00,890
<i>‪They won't be able to open fire easily.</i>

438
00:35:01,641 --> 00:35:02,850
‪Okay.

439
00:35:02,934 --> 00:35:04,143
‪That makes things simple.

440
00:35:04,227 --> 00:35:06,020
‪We're out of time. Let's do this.

441
00:35:06,646 --> 00:35:07,730
‪Let's go, master chef.

442
00:35:10,316 --> 00:35:11,651
‪Don't forget to send status updates.

443
00:35:11,734 --> 00:35:13,903
‪There's so much laundry today.

444
00:35:13,986 --> 00:35:15,113
‪Goodness me.

445
00:35:18,908 --> 00:35:19,992
‪All right.

446
00:35:34,090 --> 00:35:36,050
‪Laundry truck standing by
‪at the loading dock.

447
00:35:36,968 --> 00:35:37,885
‪Hurry up.

448
00:35:38,427 --> 00:35:41,639
‪Hey, neighbors from up north!

449
00:35:41,722 --> 00:35:43,391
‪Your security has been breached!

450
00:35:43,474 --> 00:35:45,560
‪How can it be so weak?

451
00:35:46,144 --> 00:35:47,603
‪You guys are screwed now

452
00:35:48,229 --> 00:35:49,063
‪because I'm here.

453
00:35:50,064 --> 00:35:50,982
‪Hey, Jin-cheol.

454
00:35:54,527 --> 00:35:55,611
‪Rock and roll!

455
00:36:24,348 --> 00:36:26,767
‪We each get 15 guys.

456
00:36:26,851 --> 00:36:27,852
‪Keep count, okay?

457
00:36:38,279 --> 00:36:40,823
‪-Hey, demo team!
‪-I said don't bring that up!

458
00:36:48,748 --> 00:36:49,582
‪Mr. Kim.

459
00:36:49,665 --> 00:36:51,667
‪I haven't secured
‪a clear route for you yet.

460
00:36:51,751 --> 00:36:53,002
‪The agents aren't moving.

461
00:37:02,053 --> 00:37:04,096
‪Surveillance room, anything unusual?

462
00:37:05,097 --> 00:37:06,682
‪Surveillance room, do you copy?

463
00:37:07,975 --> 00:37:09,018
‪What the hell?

464
00:37:11,854 --> 00:37:12,813
‪Follow me.

465
00:37:14,982 --> 00:37:17,109
‪Mr. Kim, they've caught on.

466
00:37:17,735 --> 00:37:19,362
‪They'll be there soon. Get out of there.

467
00:37:19,445 --> 00:37:20,613
<i>‪What about you?</i>

468
00:37:21,239 --> 00:37:22,657
‪We're out of time.

469
00:37:23,449 --> 00:37:24,742
‪We move in one minute.

470
00:38:01,195 --> 00:38:02,405
‪-Check that way.
‪-Yes, sir.

471
00:38:08,869 --> 00:38:10,454
‪That son of a bitch.

472
00:38:10,538 --> 00:38:11,914
‪He's already here.

473
00:38:13,165 --> 00:38:14,792
‪What the hell happened?

474
00:38:14,875 --> 00:38:17,795
‪Three of them came in and attacked us.

475
00:38:17,878 --> 00:38:19,130
‪Three?

476
00:38:20,006 --> 00:38:23,134
‪Secure our comms
‪and activate the jamming device right now.

477
00:38:23,217 --> 00:38:24,093
‪Yes, sir!

478
00:38:26,429 --> 00:38:27,805
‪What are you doing?

479
00:38:27,888 --> 00:38:29,557
‪Get the surveillance cameras back up now!

480
00:38:29,640 --> 00:38:30,558
‪Yes, sir!

481
00:38:38,065 --> 00:38:38,941
‪ENTER ACTIVATION CODE

482
00:38:39,025 --> 00:38:39,859
‪COMPLETE
‪ACTIVATION READY

483
00:38:43,070 --> 00:38:45,698
‪Let's cut off their communication first.

484
00:38:47,366 --> 00:38:49,660
‪Hey, Kim. How much longer until you--

485
00:38:56,083 --> 00:38:57,501
‪NO SIGNAL

486
00:38:59,503 --> 00:39:00,504
‪What's going on?

487
00:39:03,924 --> 00:39:06,719
‪What's your plan now?

488
00:39:12,808 --> 00:39:15,728
‪Hey, you guys know how to use jammers?

489
00:39:16,395 --> 00:39:17,438
‪It means the attack starts now.

490
00:39:17,521 --> 00:39:21,067
‪But they started attacking us a while ago.

491
00:39:21,150 --> 00:39:22,777
‪We can end things here if we're lucky.

492
00:39:22,860 --> 00:39:24,236
‪Did the entire North
‪come down here or what?

493
00:39:24,320 --> 00:39:25,154
‪Come on, bring it!

494
00:39:25,237 --> 00:39:26,947
‪No, just go home!

495
00:40:45,693 --> 00:40:47,570
<i>‪Emergency alert!</i>

496
00:40:51,031 --> 00:40:52,908
<i>‪An unidentified attacker is on the move.</i>

497
00:40:54,618 --> 00:40:55,995
<i>‪Move in immediately.</i>

498
00:40:56,078 --> 00:40:57,246
‪The unidentified attacker has entered

499
00:40:57,329 --> 00:40:58,873
‪the emergency stairwell
‪on the fifth floor.

500
00:41:03,127 --> 00:41:03,961
‪Take the stairs.

501
00:41:36,869 --> 00:41:39,663
‪RESTORE IN PROGRESS

502
00:41:39,747 --> 00:41:41,040
‪RESTORE COMPLETE

503
00:41:42,208 --> 00:41:43,250
‪The cameras are back up, sir.

504
00:42:00,309 --> 00:42:01,936
‪Get the EMP charge ready.

505
00:42:02,019 --> 00:42:03,103
‪Sir?

506
00:42:03,187 --> 00:42:04,396
‪You heard me!

507
00:42:12,238 --> 00:42:13,239
‪-That was me.
‪-That was me.

508
00:42:13,948 --> 00:42:15,157
‪-I took him down.
‪-I took him down.

509
00:42:15,741 --> 00:42:17,117
‪Don't be ridiculous!

510
00:42:19,328 --> 00:42:20,496
‪Did we take down about 20 of them?

511
00:42:21,121 --> 00:42:22,331
‪Yeah, sounds about right.

512
00:42:22,414 --> 00:42:26,001
‪Then let's just say
‪we each took down 10, okay?

513
00:42:27,044 --> 00:42:27,878
‪Okay.

514
00:42:28,546 --> 00:42:29,588
‪Time's almost up.

515
00:42:29,672 --> 00:42:31,048
‪Let's get going.

516
00:42:31,131 --> 00:42:32,967
‪Kim should be out of here by now.

517
00:42:34,134 --> 00:42:35,052
‪Jeez, I'm exhausted.

518
00:42:44,436 --> 00:42:45,771
‪Who are these latecomers?

519
00:42:46,272 --> 00:42:48,357
‪Couldn't you have just come all at once?

520
00:42:48,440 --> 00:42:50,276
‪We can take care of them
‪all at once this way.

521
00:42:50,901 --> 00:42:52,987
‪You've got a really
‪positive attitude sometimes.

522
00:42:54,572 --> 00:42:55,781
‪Jin-cheol, don't…

523
00:42:56,407 --> 00:42:58,117
‪Don't go in there alone, Jin-cheol.

524
00:42:58,200 --> 00:43:00,119
‪-What more is there to say?
‪-Jin-cheol!

525
00:43:00,202 --> 00:43:01,704
‪-Except with our fists.
‪-Why isn't this button working?

526
00:43:01,787 --> 00:43:03,414
‪-Come on!
‪-Jin-cheol!

527
00:43:05,249 --> 00:43:06,584
‪I guess I'll take the stairs.

528
00:43:20,431 --> 00:43:22,391
‪Seriously, what's going on?

529
00:43:24,643 --> 00:43:26,061
‪-Sir?
‪-Yes?

530
00:43:26,145 --> 00:43:26,979
‪Are you not done yet?

531
00:43:27,062 --> 00:43:29,732
‪Right, I'm almost done.

532
00:43:35,529 --> 00:43:36,697
‪Is that all you've got?

533
00:43:37,615 --> 00:43:38,741
‪Bring it on!

534
00:43:40,409 --> 00:43:42,119
‪That doesn't hurt at all!

535
00:43:46,874 --> 00:43:48,459
‪What's the range on this?

536
00:43:48,542 --> 00:43:51,045
‪It'll cut power to the whole building.

537
00:43:58,344 --> 00:44:04,475
‪WAY TO LOADING DOCK

538
00:44:07,853 --> 00:44:08,854
‪All right, all right.

539
00:44:09,563 --> 00:44:11,106
‪Hold on a second.

540
00:44:11,857 --> 00:44:13,067
‪Let's talk this out.

541
00:44:25,746 --> 00:44:27,206
‪Situation room. Come in, situation room.

542
00:44:27,289 --> 00:44:29,375
‪Check Zone 1 and the situation room.

543
00:44:36,256 --> 00:44:37,174
‪KITCHEN STORAGE

544
00:44:37,257 --> 00:44:38,092
‪Get inside.

545
00:44:47,101 --> 00:44:48,060
‪Have you looked around?

546
00:44:48,727 --> 00:44:51,313
‪I've searched everywhere
‪in the reception hall but can't find them.

547
00:44:51,397 --> 00:44:53,899
‪Where the hell
‪are those rat bastards hiding?

548
00:44:55,609 --> 00:44:57,069
‪What should we do now?

549
00:44:57,694 --> 00:44:59,530
‪Damn it, follow me.

550
00:45:01,115 --> 00:45:04,576
‪Time's up. Why aren't they here yet?

551
00:45:04,660 --> 00:45:06,453
‪-What about the electrician?
‪-They're on their way.

552
00:45:09,998 --> 00:45:10,833
‪Sir?

553
00:45:11,750 --> 00:45:13,085
‪Looks like you're done collecting.

554
00:45:13,669 --> 00:45:15,087
‪Yes, I'm done.

555
00:45:15,170 --> 00:45:17,089
‪Then you should go now. Thank you.

556
00:45:17,673 --> 00:45:19,007
‪Right.

557
00:45:19,842 --> 00:45:21,468
‪-I need to use the restroom.
‪-You can't.

558
00:45:21,552 --> 00:45:23,429
‪We have a situation inside the resort.

559
00:45:24,096 --> 00:45:25,764
‪Please make your way outside
‪for your safety.

560
00:45:25,848 --> 00:45:27,224
‪But it'll only take a minute.

561
00:45:27,307 --> 00:45:29,143
‪No, sir. Please go back now.

562
00:45:30,394 --> 00:45:31,228
‪Okay.

563
00:45:31,854 --> 00:45:33,564
‪Guess I'll have to wait until I get home.

564
00:45:36,817 --> 00:45:37,693
‪Goodbye, then.

565
00:45:53,750 --> 00:45:55,127
‪What the hell? Did the power go off?

566
00:45:55,210 --> 00:45:56,420
‪-It's me.
‪-Move!

567
00:45:56,503 --> 00:45:57,671
‪Lights!

568
00:46:04,803 --> 00:46:05,637
‪Hey.

569
00:46:05,721 --> 00:46:06,597
‪I said we should talk it out.

570
00:46:11,894 --> 00:46:12,728
‪Lights!

571
00:46:14,480 --> 00:46:15,606
‪It's me, Tae Geun.

572
00:46:17,399 --> 00:46:18,275
‪I'm Jin Bok.

573
00:46:19,109 --> 00:46:19,943
‪I'm Jin-cheol.

574
00:46:20,569 --> 00:46:21,403
‪I'm Gwang Sun.

575
00:46:22,779 --> 00:46:23,780
‪Get him!

576
00:46:24,406 --> 00:46:25,240
‪You bastard!

577
00:46:35,167 --> 00:46:36,293
‪That bastard.

578
00:46:36,919 --> 00:46:38,003
‪Where did he go?

579
00:46:49,473 --> 00:46:50,724
‪I said we should talk it out.

580
00:46:50,807 --> 00:46:52,768
‪Rock and roll!

581
00:47:07,366 --> 00:47:09,243
‪What are you doing?

582
00:47:09,326 --> 00:47:11,537
‪Go after them right now and kill them.

583
00:47:11,620 --> 00:47:15,290
‪I want you to kill
‪both 66 and Ri Eung Ryeong.

584
00:47:15,374 --> 00:47:16,250
‪Right now!

585
00:47:28,095 --> 00:47:30,305
‪KITCHEN STORAGE

586
00:47:50,784 --> 00:47:51,910
‪What happened?

587
00:48:00,377 --> 00:48:01,211
‪Run.

588
00:48:26,653 --> 00:48:29,906
‪You guys pop out of nowhere
‪like cockroaches.

589
00:48:29,990 --> 00:48:31,617
‪I didn't believe it at first,

590
00:48:31,700 --> 00:48:33,785
‪but it really is you,
‪Comrade Sung Han-soo.

591
00:48:34,661 --> 00:48:37,873
‪The sports heroes
‪from the North and the South meet again.

592
00:48:37,956 --> 00:48:40,709
‪Right, I'm indeed a hero.

593
00:48:41,335 --> 00:48:42,753
‪But I don't know who you are.

594
00:48:42,836 --> 00:48:43,879
‪Have we met before?

595
00:48:44,463 --> 00:48:46,256
‪We competed in different events,

596
00:48:46,340 --> 00:48:48,467
‪but we've run into each other
‪at the Olympics.

597
00:48:51,803 --> 00:48:53,013
‪Hey, that's scary.

598
00:48:53,096 --> 00:48:54,473
‪I don't know who you are.

599
00:48:54,556 --> 00:48:55,974
‪What was your event?

600
00:48:56,892 --> 00:48:57,893
‪Rhythmic gymnastics?

601
00:48:58,560 --> 00:49:00,479
‪You'll find out if you fight me.

602
00:49:00,562 --> 00:49:02,230
‪Just save the fighting and tell me.

603
00:49:03,440 --> 00:49:05,192
‪You don't have to tell me
‪if you don't want to.

604
00:49:05,275 --> 00:49:06,485
‪Hey.

605
00:49:06,568 --> 00:49:08,612
‪It's unfair to me
‪if you set it down there.

606
00:49:08,695 --> 00:49:10,113
‪Your mouth still works fine.

607
00:49:11,365 --> 00:49:12,658
‪The rest of my body works fine too.

608
00:49:14,826 --> 00:49:15,744
‪Bring it.

609
00:50:07,838 --> 00:50:10,882
<i>‪For Min-ji's sake, I'm going to end you.</i>

610
00:50:17,889 --> 00:50:19,391
<i>‪-Beg for my daughter's forgiveness.</i>
‪-I'm sorry.

611
00:50:19,474 --> 00:50:21,184
<i>‪With all your heart.</i>

612
00:50:45,959 --> 00:50:47,210
‪Oh, short ribs.

613
00:50:49,713 --> 00:50:50,797
‪I know now.

614
00:50:51,548 --> 00:50:55,010
‪I figured it out
‪from your moves and your ears.

615
00:50:56,803 --> 00:50:57,971
‪You wear tights, right?

616
00:50:58,054 --> 00:51:00,474
‪I'm Jang Tae San,
‪the gold medalist in wrestling.

617
00:51:01,975 --> 00:51:02,809
‪Jang Tae San.

618
00:51:04,144 --> 00:51:06,062
‪You mean…

619
00:51:06,146 --> 00:51:07,189
<i>‪the</i>‪ Jang Tae San?

620
00:51:09,065 --> 00:51:11,067
‪I didn't ask for your name
‪because I don't care.

621
00:51:18,408 --> 00:51:21,661
‪This space is too small
‪for you to show off your footwork.

622
00:51:23,497 --> 00:51:24,331
‪You want some?

623
00:51:24,873 --> 00:51:25,832
‪Here you go.

624
00:51:27,125 --> 00:51:29,127
‪You see, I run a Taekwondo studio.

625
00:51:31,546 --> 00:51:32,464
‪But sometimes,

626
00:51:33,381 --> 00:51:34,508
‪I teach judo.

627
00:51:38,970 --> 00:51:39,930
‪Bring it.

628
00:51:43,517 --> 00:51:44,601
‪What now?

629
00:51:50,315 --> 00:51:51,316
‪For crying out loud.

630
00:51:51,399 --> 00:51:53,193
‪I can't leave.

631
00:51:53,276 --> 00:51:54,486
‪I really can't leave.

632
00:52:04,454 --> 00:52:07,833
‪SPA

633
00:52:10,877 --> 00:52:12,462
‪HINOKI BATH

634
00:53:46,097 --> 00:53:47,807
‪No, no…

635
00:53:55,065 --> 00:53:55,899
‪Come out.

636
00:54:09,287 --> 00:54:10,246
‪Damn it.

637
00:55:02,924 --> 00:55:04,759
‪What are you, a blacksmith?!

638
00:55:15,061 --> 00:55:15,895
‪Just die!

639
00:55:21,735 --> 00:55:23,153
‪Man, I'm so sick of this.

640
00:55:45,008 --> 00:55:46,843
‪I'm Jang Tae San.

641
00:55:49,137 --> 00:55:50,555
‪Nobody asked.

642
00:56:08,782 --> 00:56:11,993
‪Why did I even volunteer to help?

643
00:56:15,246 --> 00:56:17,457
‪This is what they get
‪for refusing to talk it out.

644
00:56:21,336 --> 00:56:23,338
‪Park Jin-cheol, you've still got it.

645
00:56:25,173 --> 00:56:27,342
‪This is rock spirit!

646
00:56:27,425 --> 00:56:28,259
‪Man, I'm wiped.

647
00:56:55,870 --> 00:56:56,871
‪Don't move!

648
00:56:58,039 --> 00:56:59,999
‪You all know who I am!

649
00:57:00,083 --> 00:57:03,086
‪Don't move, or else we all die!

650
00:57:15,014 --> 00:57:16,224
‪Damn it.

651
00:57:16,307 --> 00:57:19,018
‪-I fought them four to one.
‪-He's not back yet.

652
00:57:20,937 --> 00:57:22,272
‪What the hell?

653
00:57:23,857 --> 00:57:25,733
‪He's a tenacious bastard.

654
00:57:26,401 --> 00:57:27,444
‪You untied yourself?

655
00:57:27,527 --> 00:57:28,987
‪How?

656
00:57:29,070 --> 00:57:30,155
‪You tied him, didn't you?

657
00:57:30,238 --> 00:57:32,031
‪You tied… Oh, it was me.

658
00:57:32,115 --> 00:57:33,199
‪-Hey.
‪-Hey, get over here.

659
00:57:33,283 --> 00:57:34,576
<i>‪Mister.</i>

660
00:57:34,659 --> 00:57:36,578
<i>‪Why are you doing this to us?</i>

661
00:57:38,413 --> 00:57:40,540
<i>‪Please let us go.</i>

662
00:57:41,374 --> 00:57:43,585
<i>‪Untie us right now!</i>

663
00:57:43,668 --> 00:57:44,752
<i>‪Mister,</i>

664
00:57:44,836 --> 00:57:46,838
<i>‪please let us go.</i>

665
00:57:48,131 --> 00:57:49,674
<i>‪Please!</i>

666
00:57:51,718 --> 00:57:53,636
‪You asshole!

667
00:57:58,266 --> 00:58:00,310
‪If you so much as lay a finger on me…

668
00:58:02,562 --> 00:58:03,396
‪your kids are dead.

669
00:58:09,611 --> 00:58:11,070
‪Jin-cheol, let go.

670
00:58:12,530 --> 00:58:13,907
‪Let go!

671
00:58:43,228 --> 00:58:44,646
‪If anything happens to Da-bin,

672
00:58:45,647 --> 00:58:48,358
‪I'm going to chew you up.

673
00:58:56,783 --> 00:58:57,617
‪Our kids…

674
00:58:59,619 --> 00:59:00,828
‪Where are they?

675
00:59:53,756 --> 00:59:57,427
‪AGENT KIM REACTIVATED

676
00:59:58,094 --> 00:59:58,970
<i>‪Kim.</i>

677
00:59:59,971 --> 01:00:01,014
<i>‪If you don't come,</i>

678
01:00:01,848 --> 01:00:03,057
<i>‪the kids will die.</i>

679
01:00:06,019 --> 01:00:08,062
<i>‪If 66 dies, the kids will live.</i>

680
01:00:08,146 --> 01:00:09,564
<i>‪Do you really have a choice?</i>

681
01:00:09,647 --> 01:00:10,940
<i>‪I'll give you five minutes.</i>

682
01:00:12,442 --> 01:00:14,402
<i>‪Protecting the people I care about…</i>

683
01:00:14,485 --> 01:00:16,154
<i>‪I'll shoot the kids myself.</i>

684
01:00:16,237 --> 01:00:18,072
‪Then I'll shoot 66.

685
01:00:18,156 --> 01:00:19,240
<i>‪Please take care…</i>

686
01:00:21,159 --> 01:00:22,243
‪of Min-ji.

687
01:00:22,785 --> 01:00:23,620
<i>‪Number 66…</i>

688
01:00:26,372 --> 01:00:27,206
<i>‪must die.</i>

689
01:00:30,501 --> 01:00:33,504
‪Subtitle translation by:
